<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="051" project="spaarke-project-coordination-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Router: critical-area acknowledgement gate with stale-ack removal (FR-22)</title>
    <phase>5 Resolution and critical areas</phase>
    <gate>035 complete; D-1 agreed with ci-cd-unit-test-remediation-r1 (or the owner) before merge</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Adds blocking behaviour to the only required master check.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Changes the required Router check that every PR passes; a mistake blocks or unblocks the whole repo.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P5-A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>035</deps>
    <tags>ci-cd, devops, testing, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6-8 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Fold a critical-area acknowledgement into Router. A PR touching a critical area owned by another active project fails until it carries the ack label, which the owning project's session applies after review. A later push that changes critical-area files removes ack. Everything else is unchanged.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE CI developer. GitHub Actions, the ci-router.yml classify/router-result structure.</role>
  <goal>ci-router.yml enforces the rule, the fixtures pass, and Router behaves identically for PRs with no critical-area touch.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-22, C-6 (fold into Router; no ruleset change), C-10 (autonomous: the owning project's session applies ack), A-4 (stale ack removed). Critical-area globs are in .claude/constraints/cross-session.md section B; owners come from README frontmatter via project_registry.py. D-1: Router's docs_only skip stays with ci-cd-unit-test-remediation-r1; agree this change with them before merge.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">.github/workflows/ci-router.yml</file>
      <file role="new">scripts/quality/critical-area-ack.py</file>
      <file role="new">scripts/quality/tests/test_critical_area_ack.py</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <justification>
    <existing>Router (ci-router.yml router-result job) is the single required master check; classify computes docs_only and path flags.</existing>
    <extension>Folded in: a new step in Router's flow, not a new required check (C-6). The decision logic is a script so it can be tested with fixtures; the workflow only calls it.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A PR merges into another project's auth or access-control code unseen (E5).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec FR-22">Scope: critical-area-ack.py takes the PR's changed paths, labels and author branch, plus the registry, and returns fail when a changed path matches a critical-area glob that lies inside an owned_areas glob of another project whose lifecycle is active, and the PR lacks ack. It returns pass with ack, advisory (pass plus a summary line) for non-critical owned areas, and pass when the owner is paused, closed or unregistered.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec FR-22, A-4">Scope: on a pull_request synchronize event, if the new commits change any critical-area path and the PR has ack, the workflow removes ack (gh pr edit --remove-label) and the check fails until it is re-applied.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec FR-22 negatives">Scope: no ruleset change; no comment parsing; Router's verdict is unchanged for PRs with no critical-area touch; docs_only handling is untouched. Only the job that edits labels gets pull-requests: write.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the ack check runs on pull_request only. push and merge_group events skip it and keep today's behaviour.</constraint>
    <constraint source="escalation-boundary">Scope: this task does not merge until D-1 is recorded in notes/decisions.md.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-project-coordination-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/cross-session.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/ci-cd/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Router structure" location=".github/workflows/ci-router.yml">classify outputs feed router-result; add the ack result as one more input to the decision summary.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Registry reader" location="scripts/quality/project_registry.py">Owners and lifecycle.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read ci-router.yml in full; note in the task notes where the ack step joins the router-result decision.</step>
    <step order="2">Write critical-area-ack.py and its fixtures.</step>
    <step order="3">Wire it into the workflow, with the stale-ack removal on synchronize.</step>
    <step order="4">Run the tests and actionlint; open a draft PR touching a fixture-only critical path to watch Router fail, apply ack, and watch it pass. Record the run URLs.</step>
    <step order="5">Record D-1 agreement in notes/decisions.md before marking the PR ready.</step>
    <step order="6">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task to ✅ [done] AND set this POML status to completed; run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If ci-cd-unit-test-remediation-r1 (or the owner, if that project is closed) does not agree to the Router change, STOP before merge and escalate (spec D-1).</trigger>
    <trigger>If any existing Router test or fixture changes outcome, STOP and escalate rather than adjusting the fixture.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">.github/workflows/ci-router.yml</output>
    <output type="code">scripts/quality/critical-area-ack.py</output>
    <output type="test">scripts/quality/tests/test_critical_area_ack.py</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Fixture: an un-acked PR touching another active project's critical area → fail.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Fixture: the same PR with ack → pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Fixture: a non-critical owned area → pass with an advisory line.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Fixture: the owner paused, closed or unregistered → pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Fixture: the project's own critical area → pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A synchronize event changing critical-area files on an acked PR removes ack, and the check then fails.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a PR with no critical-area touch gets the same Router verdict as before (fixture comparison); docs_only handling unchanged; no ruleset change.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract and the edge cases above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Seeding proof: invert the ack check once and confirm the un-acked fixture passes (test fails), then restore it. This gate guards cross-project auth and access code.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting this task, load all files listed in the knowledge files. Follow the task-execute skill for the mandatory pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
